From 42c0902476827718a484622b918ad24c25dfb02e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emilien Guenichon <e.guenichon@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 07:06:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] llama.cpp: add Fable 5 optimizations - mmap pinning + MoE
 expert prefetch

Patch 1: Pin mmap-backed CPU weights for faster H2D uploads
- Wire up dead GGML_CUDA_REGISTER_HOST code path
- After model load, cudaHostRegister the mmap pages backing
  weights kept in system memory
- Opt-in via GGML_CUDA_REGISTER_HOST=1
- Ornith 9B Q5_K_M: +135% prefill (-ngl 0), +57% prefill (-ngl 20)

Patch 2+3: Overlap offloaded expert weight uploads with compute
- Full-tensor prefetch of MUL_MAT_ID weights through 2nd backend
- Event-ordered staging slots overlap uploads with compute
- Default 3 slots (one MoE layer), configurable via
  GGML_SCHED_PREFETCH_EXPERTS=N
- Fixes: bounds check in register_host(), full prefetch_used reset,
  prefetch_cur reset on disable

Based on analysis by Claude Fable 5, adapted from
https://github.com/thecodacus/llama.cpp (branches fable5/*)
Verified output token-identical to mainline
